.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/tailwindcss/src/postcss-plugins/nesting Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "tailwindcss/nesting"
.PP
This is a PostCSS plugin that wraps \fRpostcss-nested\fP or \fRpostcss-nesting\fP and acts as a compatibility layer to make sure your nesting plugin of choice properly understands Tailwind's custom syntax like \fR@apply\fP and \fR@screen\fP\&.

.PP
Add it to your PostCSS configuration, somewhere before Tailwind itself:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// postcss\&.config\&.js
module\&.exports = {
  plugins: [
    require('postcss\-import'),
    require('tailwindcss/nesting'),
    require('tailwindcss'),
    require('autoprefixer'),
  ]
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
By default, it uses the \fRpostcss-nested\fP plugin under the hood, which uses a Sass-like syntax and is the plugin that powers nesting support in the \fRTailwind CSS plugin API\fP\&.

.PP
If you'd rather use \fRpostcss-nesting\fP (which is based on the work-in-progress \fRCSS Nesting\fP specification), first install the plugin alongside:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install postcss\-nesting
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then pass the plugin itself as an argument to \fRtailwindcss/nesting\fP in your PostCSS configuration:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// postcss\&.config\&.js
module\&.exports = {
  plugins: [
    require('postcss\-import'),
    require('tailwindcss/nesting')(require('postcss\-nesting')),
    require('tailwindcss'),
    require('autoprefixer'),
  ]
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
This can also be helpful if for whatever reason you need to use a very specific version of \fRpostcss-nested\fP and want to override the version we bundle with \fRtailwindcss/nesting\fP itself\&. 
